{:edb/db-before-t 777 :edb/db-after-t 778 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534090 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:50:22.311Z" 13194139534090 true] [17592186087385 1145 "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(t) &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dt}(-6t - 3t^{2}) \\\\\n&=-6 - 6t \\\\\n&=-6(1 + t)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534090 false] [17592186087385 1145 "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186087386 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv(t) &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dt}(1 + 2t + 3t^{2} + 4t^{3}) \\\\\n&= 2 + 6t + 12t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(t) &= \\frac{dv}{dt} \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dt}(2 + 6t + 12t^{2}) \\\\\n&= 6 + 24t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(0) &= 6 + 24(0) \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$." 13194139534090 false] [17592186087386 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$." 13194139534090 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277239 13194139534090 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277246 13194139534090 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277253 13194139534090 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277256 13194139534090 true] [17592186087828 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277259 13194139534090 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277262 13194139534090 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277265 13194139534090 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277269 13194139534090 true] [17592186087829 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277272 13194139534090 true] [17592186088036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534090 true] [17592186088036 1100 "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t) = 4t^{3} + 10t^{2} - 15$, where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t = 3$ seconds." 13194139534090 false] [17592186088036 1100 "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=3$ seconds." 13194139534090 true] [17592186088036 1145 "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}+20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}+20t) \\\\  & =24t+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=3$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =24(3)+20 \\\\  & =72+20 \\\\  & =92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=3$ seconds is $92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277240 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1089 "q-102616" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1100 "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t).$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1113 #uuid "fb90cea8-c194-5f3c-8376-493a94dba4ab" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277239 1145 "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+4 \\\\  & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=6,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)} & ={e}^{1} \\\\ t & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=e,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =(e\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+4e) \\\\  & =e(1)+4e \\\\  & =5e\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $5e\\text{ m/s}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277241 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277242 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277243 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277244 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277245 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1041 "selection" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277243 13194139534090 true] [17592186277240 1110 #uuid "634c92dc-28e2-5d94-a251-4d66982ec073" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277241 1034 "5\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277241 1111 #uuid "89626065-c358-5daa-bfdb-9e9ad965be20" 13194139534090 true] [1759218627724