{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-1\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277248 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277249 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277250 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277251 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277252 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1041 "selection" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277250 13194139534090 true] [17592186277247 1110 #uuid "4cd1abc5-3394-5abf-95f2-d520b095aff0" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277248 1034 "-3\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277248 1111 #uuid "fe2c33dc-a25e-5115-821d-2a488578c7c6" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277249 1034 "1\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277249 1111 #uuid "00589345-22ca-5843-9e6f-7da2c12880b8" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277250 1034 "-1\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277250 1111 #uuid "374a0e08-4030-591f-b937-d9f89ca1de5f" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277251 1034 "2\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277251 1111 #uuid "9fa23b08-3989-592a-a7ca-6b270f384213" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277252 1034 "3\\text{ m/s}" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277252 1111 #uuid "a339a6f0-0f50-5a18-a092-07b100d1f732" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277254 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1089 "q-315537" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1100 "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhen $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1113 #uuid "fa61f090-9a51-53fc-9eb9-ce631e6c3c5c" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277253 1145 "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2t+1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7} & =2t+1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7})}^{2} & ={(2t+1)}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+7 & =4{t}^{2}+4t+1 \\\\ 0 & =3{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ 0 & ={t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ 0 & =(t-1)(t+2) \\\\ t & =1,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $t=1$ since $t\\ge 0.$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=1,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+7} \\\\  & =3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=3\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277255 13194139534090 true] [17592186277254 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534090 true] [17592186277254 1041 "field-1" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277254 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277255 13194139534090 true] [17592186277254 1110 #uuid "bd921af4-aae4-5aef-a9bc-38b09efbfd86" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277255 1034 "3" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534090 true] [17592186277255 1111 #uuid "c0943335-10f4-58f4-a867-9fc0124f9f86" 13194139534090 true] [17592186277256 1017 #edb/ref 175921862772